General elections were held in [[Ecuador]] on 20 October 2002, with a second round of the presidential elections on 24 November.<ref name=N1>[[Dieter Nohlen]] (2005) ''Elections in the Americas: A data handbook, Volume II'', p380 {{ISBN|978-0-19-928358-3}}</ref> The result was a victory for [[Lucio Gutiérrez]] of the [[Patriotic Society Party|PSP]]–[[Pachakutik Plurinational Unity Movement – New Country|MUPP–NP]] alliance, who won the run-off with 54.8% of the vote.<ref>Nohlen, p404</ref> The [[Social Christian Party (Ecuador)|Social Christian Party]] emerged as the largest party in the [[National Congress (Ecuador)|National Congress]], winning 24 of the 100 seats.<ref>[http://www.ipu.org/parline-e/reports/arc/2095_02.htm Elections held in 2002] IPU</ref>

